config:
  flowchart:
    wrappingWidth: 400
---
flowchart TB
  accTitle: How the caller speaks with a voice pack
  accDescr: A voice pack is a folder of autodarts/voices in the media folder, either a pack of darts-caller copied there or one that autodarts.generate_voice_pack recorded with a text-to-speech engine such as Piper. For every call, the scoreboard looks for the files of the call in the pack, such as 180, busted, gameshot or yr_40. When the pack has them, the screen loads them from Home Assistant with its login and plays them one after the other, with a name the pack lacks in the browser's voice. When the pack lacks the call, or a file does not load, the browser's voice says the whole call. Either way, the next call waits until this one has ended.

  COPY["A pack of darts-caller,<br/>copied to the media folder"] --> FOLDER["/media/autodarts/voices/russ-bray"]
  GENERATE["autodarts.generate_voice_pack<br/>records one with Piper"] --> FOLDER
  CALL["A call: 180, a bust, a game shot,<br/>the match, you require 40"] --> FILES{{"Has the pack its files?<br/>180, busted, gameshot,<br/>matchshot, yr_40"}}
  FOLDER --> FILES
  FILES -- "yes" --> PLAY["The screen loads them with its login<br/>and plays them one after the other;<br/>a name without a file in the browser's voice"]
  FILES -- "no" --> BROWSER["The browser's voice<br/>says the whole call"]
  PLAY -- "a file does not load" --> BROWSER
  PLAY --> NEXT["The next call waits<br/>until this one has ended"]
  BROWSER --> NEXT

  classDef bot fill:#526cfe2e,stroke:#526cfe,stroke-width:2px
  classDef done fill:#16a34a2e,stroke:#16a34a,stroke-width:2px
  classDef warn fill:#f59e0b2e,stroke:#f59e0b,stroke-width:2px
  class FOLDER,FILES bot
  class PLAY,NEXT done
  class BROWSER warn
